#====================================================================
# DRAFT-libplctag-2.6.5-ohos-pthread-cancel-android-branch-mirror
# 触发事件: libplctag 2.6.5 HarmonyOS PC 适配（R01）
#          ld.lld: undefined symbol: pthread_cancel
#          上游 platform.c thread_kill() 调用 pthread_cancel，
#          OHOS musl libc 不提供该符号；上游已有 __ANDROID__ 替代分支
#====================================================================

id:                     DRAFT-libplctag-2.6.5-ohos-pthread-cancel-android-branch-mirror
trigger_tool:           clang|ld|conan|cmake|make
phase:                  linking|compilation
error_signature: 'undefined symbol: pthread_cancel|undefined reference to pthread_cancel|pthread_cancel.*implicit-function-declaration'

severity:               2
category:               platform, compat, libc, musl, threading
match_keywords:         pthread_cancel, pthread_kill, __ANDROID__, __OHOS__,
                         musl, threading, thread cancellation, platform guard,
                         undefined symbol, libplctag, thread_kill

title: 'OHOS: mirror upstream __ANDROID__ pthread_cancel fallback via platform guard extension'

root_cause: >
  OHOS musl libc does not implement POSIX thread cancellation
  (pthread_cancel/pthread_testcancel/pthread_setcancelstate). Upstream code that
  guards a pthread_kill fallback under `#ifdef __ANDROID__` and otherwise calls
  pthread_cancel fails to link on OHOS with `undefined symbol: pthread_cancel` in
  the non-Android path (e.g. libplctag src/platform/posix/platform.c
  thread_kill()). This differs from E127 (undef macro for OpenMP) and E513
  (signal-based exit) in that the upstream source already ships an Android-valid
  fallback that only needs its preprocessor guard widened.

solution: >
  Extend the existing Android guard to also match OHOS instead of introducing a
  new signal scheme: change
    #ifdef __ANDROID__
        pthread_kill(t->p_thread, 0);
    #else
        pthread_cancel(t->p_thread);
    #endif
  to
    #if defined(__ANDROID__) || defined(__OHOS__)
        pthread_kill(t->p_thread, 0);
    #else
        pthread_cancel(t->p_thread);
    #endif
  Patch form: patches/0001-src-platform-posix-platform.c.patch (portability).
  Keep semantics identical to the shipped Android branch; do not weaken the
  non-Android path. Document in conandata.yml patch_description why the guard
  is widened (R8 platform-macro exception: musl libc probe).

verification_cmd: >
  python3 scripts/ohc-run.py conan-verify libplctag 2.6.5
  (G2 conan create PASS; test_package ohos_test 5x create/destroy PASS;
   nm libplctag_static.a | grep -c pthread_cancel -> 0 after patch)